  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="2fb30075-a46f-54b6-9374-0b6c1c9373ed" activityNameId="e71d0c49-87de-58c7-b7cc-2ed91c5fd357" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, ventilation system, Geschäftshaus B, Esslingen</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, ventilation system, Geschäftshaus B, Esslingen
Disposal of a ventilation system for an office building with offices only (no kitchen, restaurant or car park). The inventory is based on a building with a total heated gross floor area of 2472 m2 and a total nominal air flow of 5700 m3/h, total weight of the components: 2815 kg/Unit, building with a specific air flow rate of 2.3 m3/h per m2 heated gross floor area. Data from call of bid including components for air handling units, ducts including insulation, air valves, roof-hoods, dampers, fire dampers, silencers. The data represent a ductwork mainly made of galvanized steel and includes air handling units mainly with heat recovery. System with central air handling units.Ground heat exchanger of building not included (is part of the concrete construction).;
UUID: 820bc149-bee7-4c6b-953f-cbc5aa6e0e69
Transport to dismantling facilities, machines for handling in sorting plant, electricity demand for sorting plant, final disposal of waste material. Cut-off to recycling for metals.
Location: Specific to the technology mix encountered in sorting plants in Switzerland.
Technology: Disposal to a sorting plant assumed. Metal pieces, copper in cables and electronic devices are recycled, plastic parts are incinerated, inert wastes (e.g. rock wool) are landfilled.
Time period: Amount of material investigated in 2013. Disposal technology mix as used in late 1990ies
Production volume: na
Sampling: Waste-specific calculation based on production input data 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_820bc149-bee7-4c6b-953f-cbc5aa6e0e69.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
